{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Phase 1 RCA — confirmed defect (no repair performed)\n\nProven root cause\n`src/rebar/llm/plan_review/pin_health.py:125-180` derives related-material health by computing only the latest fingerprint and classifying every unequal pin as `stale-pin-drift` at lines 165-166. Its public delegation in `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/attest.py:50-61` supplies only `current_material_fingerprint`. This omits the full-hash compatibility already applied to the reviewed ticket itself by `_legacy_material_ok` at `attest.py:593-670`, which recognizes both superseded fingerprint generations while still rejecting real edits. Consequently, an unchanged prerequisite pinned under the post-330c/pre-2be7 generation is falsely marked drifted after commit `1afdbbd0be` changed insignificant-whitespace normalization.\n\nDiscriminating runtime proof\nUsing the retired attestation pin for canonical prerequisite `ae96-f114-5363-4d57` (`6b113a084820af9d`), a `sys.settrace` execution of `attest.derive_plan_material_pin_health(..., enforced=True)` observed `pin_health.derive_health` compute latest `current=bbe91c054a677441` and take the line-165 inequality branch, returning aggregate and target `stale-pin-drift`. Recomputing the SAME current ticket state yielded pre-330c `d39605b03b9a7f3e` and post-330c/pre-2be7 `6b113a084820af9d`; `_legacy_material_ok` returned true. Thus the historical pin exactly matches a supported full fingerprint generation for the resolved target. A negative valid-hex control pin `0000000000000000` returned `_legacy_material_ok=false` and remained `stale-pin-drift`.\n\nRivals rejected\nThe prerequisite last event is `1786100248773305001-...-SIGNATURE.json`; the dependent review was signed at `1786115382183702000`, about 4.2 hours later, with no intervening or later prerequisite event. This rejects hidden/repaired state mutation and genuine event drift. Canonical ID `ae96-f114-5363-4d57` was carried through the runtime call and produced the exact historical-generation hash, rejecting wrong target resolution. The false status is therefore fingerprint-generation drift, not plan-material drift.\n\nDefect legitimacy\nClassification: `defect`. Authority `jira-reb-1160` says related pins invalidate after related plan-material drift, while unchanged material is the causal boundary. `convulsive-calx-yearling` explicitly requires failed-sign recovery to succeed when own and review-time related material remain current. `ethnogenic-forbidden-umbrette` independently requires positively detected genuine dependency drift/loss to invalidate unconditionally. Full-hash compatibility satisfies both contracts: accept a supported historical generation only when its recomputation from CURRENT material matches byte-for-byte; otherwise remain stale.\n\nCaller-dependency gate\nExpected post-fix behavior: a pin matching the latest or any supported historical full-fingerprint generation of the current related ticket is `current`; a pin matching none remains `stale-pin-drift`; missing and malformed behavior is unchanged. Bounded sweep: `derive_health` has one production wrapper (`attest.py:50-61`), used by `compute_validity` (`attest.py:414`) and re-sign (`resign.py:261`). Their next-level consumers are claim/close/reuse/drift-refresh/bugfix-size gates plus audit/detail renderers. These are incidental consumers of the health contract: accepting unchanged material is required, and all still reject a genuine unmatched hash. No behavioral dependency on the false generation-drift result was found. Direct own-material users of `current_material_fingerprint` are outside the changed behavior and already use the legacy guard where attestation validity requires it.\n\nFrozen RED contract card\n```yaml\nauthoritative_contract: \"Related pins invalidate only after actual related plan-material drift (jira-reb-1160); recovery succeeds when review-time related material remains current (convulsive-calx-yearling); a genuine dependency edit always invalidates (ethnogenic-forbidden-umbrette).\"\ntrigger_preconditions: \"In an ephemeral real ticket store, create a readable canonical related ticket whose latest fingerprint differs from its post-330c/pre-2be7 recomputation; construct a PlanMaterialPin from that historical recomputation without changing the ticket afterward. Prove latest != pinned and historical recomputation == pinned before exercising health.\"\nproduction_path: \"In-process unit through attest.derive_plan_material_pin_health, real pin_health.derive_health, and real current_material_fingerprint_impl against the ephemeral store. One tier lower with a stub fingerprint is insufficient because it cannot exercise the generation-compatibility seam.\"\ntest_tier: \"In-process unit test, parameterized for supported historical full-fingerprint generations where fixtures permit.\"\nobservable_postcondition: \"The unchanged historical-generation pin yields target and aggregate pin_status=current under enforcement; after a semantic material edit, the same pin yields target and aggregate pin_status=stale-pin-drift.\"\nnegative_control: \"Semantically edit the ephemeral related ticket so its latest and every supported historical recomputation differ from the signed pin; assert stale-pin-drift. Also retain malformed/missing cases unchanged.\"\nci_gate: \"Exact pytest node collected and executed without skip/xfail under the focused plan-material-pin unit suite, then the repository make test gate.\"\n```\nExisting coverage inventory: `tests/unit/test_plan_material_pin_health.py` proves latest-generation current and legacy-unpinned behavior; `tests/unit/test_plan_material_pin_health_heldout.py` proves ordinary unmatched drift, enforcement/advisory behavior, missing targets, and compute-validity propagation. Neither covers a valid pin from a superseded fingerprint generation, so the RED oracle should strengthen this health suite rather than duplicate a higher-level claim fixture.\n\nPhase boundary\nPhase 1 Stages 2-3 are complete. No production or test files were edited, no RED test was created or run, and Phase 2 was not entered."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786298228212220001,"uuid":"31df2185-54c2-4235-8ab0-41410a5c522c"}